{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For you are able to do all things</b> — like: יָכוֹל תּוּכַל (you are able, you are able). Similarly: אִם שׁוֹב תָּשׁוּבוּ (if returning you return [Jeremiah 42:14]). The correct interpretation: you are able to do all things, and nothing is withheld from you, for the first [word] draws itself and another along with it."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:41.631960169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}